      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Circuit QED made the interaction of individual artificial atoms and microwave photons a controllable laboratory reality, opening a durable regime of quantum optics and information physics.",
        "attribution": "Blais supplied a decisive theoretical formulation, while Wallraff and Schoelkopf led defining experimental realizations; Girvin's conceptual contributions are also substantial.",
        "maturity": "The physics has been reproduced and elaborated across many platforms and laboratories, with a central role in modern superconducting quantum science.",
