      "proposed_laureates": [
        "Yakir Aharonov",
        "Michael V. Berry"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The Aharonov-Bohm effect and geometric phase exposed phase as an observable and physically active aspect of quantum mechanics, with far-reaching consequences.",
        "attribution": "Aharonov is central to the electromagnetic-potential effect, and Berry independently identified the general adiabatic geometric phase.",
        "maturity": "Both effects are firmly established experimentally and deeply integrated into quantum theory and condensed-matter physics.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The two discoveries are closely related in physical meaning but historically distinct, making their joint prize framing nontrivial."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 8,
